      "name": "The Cairn",
      "description": "The rock gives out into a flat crown of hill and the wind has it all to itself. A cairn of grey stone stands here shoulder-high, and it is full of things: a boot, a comb, a snapped arrow, a tin cup, a dozen small objects wedged into the gaps and gone green with weather. An old woman sits on the lee side of it with her hands in her sleeves. She watches you arrive and does not get up.",
