            {
              "action": "describe",
              "parameters": [
                "'You came up,' she says. 'Most don't. There's nothing up here and it's a bad wind.'\n\nShe does not give a name and does not seem to be waiting for anything. 'I keep the cairn. People go down that cave with everything they own, and they come back up with a key, or they don't come back up.'\n\nShe nods at the pale stones down in the hollow — the ones that spell TOGETHER when you look at them from the ledge. 'Two people put those there. I have watched this valley a long time and I have never yet seen two of you in it on the same day. You all come through it alone and you all do the same brave stupid thing alone, and then the ones who live walk out of that door and I never find out which.' She puts her hands back in her sleeves. 'If you're carrying something you don't need, I'll take it off you.'"
